data: {"id":"chatcmpl-20261007051947383842136c955d568epCKYkwY","created":1791350387,"object":"chat.completion.chunk","model":"glm-5.3-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_9f5372f70ac947178c2ef6d1","index":0,"type":"function","function":{"name":"Write","arguments":"{\"content\":\"# Cutover & Rollback Plan\\n\\n## Overview\\n\\nThis document describes the cutover procedure for the database migration and the\\nrollback plan if the cutover fails or post-cutover validation detects problems.\\n\\n**Preconditions**\\n\\n- Baseline captured in `baseline.json` (pre-migration engine/version/schema/snapshot).\\n- Old state recorded in `old_state.json`; expected target state in `new_state.json`.\\n- Dual read/write simulation (`dual_rw.sh`) has been running cleanly — see `dual_rw.log`.\\n- Shadow comparison (`shadow_compare.py old_state.json new_state.json`) reviewed and accepted.\\n- Replication is healthy per `lag_drift.txt` (small lag, no drift).\\n\\n## Cutover Steps\\n\\n1. **Verify replication health**\\n   Confirm replication lag is minimal and no drift is detected (reference values\\n   in `lag_drift.txt`). If lag is high or drift is flagged, do not proceed.\\n\\n2. **Final shadow comparison**\\n   Re-run `python3 shadow_compare.py old_state.json new_state.json` and confirm\\n   the key differences match the approved migration plan.\\n\\n3. **Freeze writes**\\n   Run `./freeze.sh`. This creates `frozen.flag` and prints `Writes frozen`.\\n   Downstream writers must treat the presence of `frozen.flag` as a stop signal.\\n\\n4. **Final data sync**\\n   Allow the replica to catch up while writes are frozen. Verify lag reaches ~0\\n   and drift remains `false`; update `lag_drift.txt` with the observed values.\\n\\n5. **Switch over traffic**\\n   Repoint reads and writes to the new system. Update connection strings /\\n   routing configuration as required.\\n\\n6. **Resume dual read/write**\\n   Run `./dual_rw.sh` a few times to log successful dual-mode operations in\\n   `dual_rw.log` during the observation window.\\n\\n7. **Validate the new state**\\n   Confirm the live state matches `new_state.json` (version, schema, snapshot id).\\n\\n8. **Record the new baseline**\\n   Archive the post-migration state as the new baseline for future migrations.\\n\\n## Rollback Plan\\n\\nTrigger rollback if any of the following occur: cutover step fails, shadow\\ncomparison shows unexpected differences, post-cutover validation fails, or\\napplication errors indicate data incompatibility.\\n\\n**Rollback steps**\\n\\n1. **Freeze writes on the new system**\\n   Run `./freeze.sh` there (create the frozen flag) to stop further changes.\\n\\n2. **Repoint traffic to the old system**\\n   Restore the original connection strings / routing configuration so reads and\\n   writes go back to the pre-migration state described in `old_state.json`.\\n\\n3. **Restore data from the pre-migration snapshot**\\n   If any writes occurred on the new system during the observation window,\\n   reconcile or restore from `data_snapshot` recorded in `baseline.json`.\\n\\n4. **Remove the frozen flag on the old system**\\n   `rm -f frozen.flag` (in the old system's directory) to unfreeze writes.\\n\\n5. **Resume dual read/write verification**\\n   Run `./dual_rw.sh` repeatedly and inspect `dual_rw.log` to confirm the old\\n   system is serving traffic normally.\\n\\n6. **Document the incident**\\n   Record what failed, when, and the observed lag/drift values to improve the\\n   next cutover attempt.\\n\\n## Residue Check\\n\\nAfter any cutover attempt (successful or rolled back), check for residue:\\nfiles left behind or modified by the procedure within the last 10 minutes.\\n\\n```bash\\nfind . -type f -mmin -10 -print\\n```\\n\\n- `-type f` — only regular files (skip directories)\\n- `-mmin -10` — modified less than 10 minutes ago\\n- `-print` — list matching paths\\n\\nRun this from the migration directory (or scope it to a specific path, e.g.\\n`find /home/agent/workspace/migration -type f -mmin -10 -print`) and review\\nthe output for unexpected leftovers such as stray flag files (`frozen.flag`),\\npartial logs, or temporary artifacts before declaring the procedure complete.\\n\",\"file_path\":\"/home/agent/workspace/migration/cutover_rollback.md\"}"}}]}}]}

